  "narrative": "The batch clarifies three things: technical-context robustness for the central associations, additional specificity for the TP53-loss/USP7 association, and mostly null broad probes.  The KY-library checks are strong for SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2 dependency and KEAP1 loss/NFE2L2 dependency: the signed estimates are +0.816 (95% interval +0.777 to +0.856) and +0.794 (+0.752 to +0.837), respectively.  Both intervals are entirely and far above the +0.10 clinically meaningful benchmark, so I accept these as within-dataset technical robustness checks supporting the already independently validated central claims H8 and H20.  For USP7, the KY TP53-loss effect is directionally consistent with the validated central H15 but less certain: signed estimate +0.212 with interval +0.051 to +0.373.  The lower bound falls below +0.10, so I do not accept the KY-stratum claim itself; I keep it unresolved/deferred.  This should not be read as contradiction of the validated TP53/USP7 central claim, but it does caution that library-context estimates can be smaller and noisier in the smaller KY subset.\n\nThe MTAP/TP53 partitioning now more strongly argues against a generic MTAP/9p21 explanation for the USP7 association.  The new MTAP tests are clinically uninformative in the hypothesized positive direction: H71 MDM2/MTAP among TP53-loss screens has signed +0.006 (-0.053 to +0.065), and H72 USP7/MTAP among CDKN2A-intact screens has signed -0.003 (-0.054 to +0.047).  Together with the prior overall MTAP, TP53-intact MTAP, TP53-loss MTAP, and TP53-by-MTAP interaction results, these all fail to show clinically meaningful positive MTAP effects.  I therefore also reassess the earlier secondary MTAP checks to reject/closed.  This is not a causal dissection of 9p21 deletion: MTAP and TP53 are co-occurring features, and some intervals are wide.  The conclusion is limited to this dataset: MTAP loss does not provide a simple independent positive predictor of USP7 or MDM2 dependency in the tested strata, while the TP53-loss/USP7 association remains the robust central signal.\n\nThe new exploratory probes are near-null.  MYC amplification is not clinically associated with TMED10 dependency (H74 signed +0.009, -0.014 to +0.031).  The MAPK cross-tests are also not clinically meaningful: KRAS mutation does not show weaker EGFR dependency (H75 signed -0.010, interval upper +0.008), and EGFR amplification does not show a clinically meaningful stronger KRAS dependency (H76 signed +0.009, interval upper +0.037).  The high-prevalence research marker screens are null for their assigned outcomes: marker D/WRN signed +0.012 (-0.011 to +0.035), marker E/SMARCA2 signed +0.006 (-0.026 to +0.038), marker F/USP7 signed -0.019 (-0.054 to +0.015), and marker F/NFE2L2 signed -0.006 (-0.038 to +0.026).  In all cases the signed intervals do not reach the +0.10 benchmark, and many point estimates are opposite the registered direction or close to zero.  I reject and close these as unsupported dataset-level hypotheses, not as proof that these markers have zero effect in every possible context.\n\nI do not request independent validation.  The four central accepted associations are already independently validated, and the newly accepted KY robustness checks are context confirmations rather than new central discoveries.  The unresolved KY USP7 check is not worth a validation slot because it is secondary and already supported in attenuated form by the validated central TP53/USP7 claim.  I registered a KY-library WRN/MSI-high comparison to complete the four-outcome technical robustness grid.",
  "research_notes": "Central independently validated accepted dataset associations: MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency; TP53 loss -> much weaker USP7 dependency. Research marker F/STAT3 is validated null and closed. New KY-library robustness: accepted for SMARCA4/SMARCA2 (+0.816, lower +0.777) and KEAP1/NFE2L2 (+0.794, lower +0.752). KY USP7/TP53 is directionally supportive but unresolved/deferred because lower bound +0.051 is below +0.10. MTAP/CDKN2A/MDM2/USP7 specificity: positive MTAP hypotheses are rejected overall and in TP53-intact/TP53-loss/CDKN2A-intact strata, as are TP53-by-MTAP interaction positive hypotheses; this supports TP53-specific dataset association more than generic MTAP loss, though not causal separation. Broad probes rejected as clinically uninformative: TMED10/MYC, KRAS mutation/EGFR dependency, EGFR amplification/KRAS dependency, marker D/WRN, marker E/SMARCA2, marker F/USP7, marker F/NFE2L2. Pending useful follow-up: KY WRN/MSI-high to complete technical robustness grid; H77 TMED10/STK11 remains active but speculative. All conclusions remain dataset-level associations, not causal mechanisms or external generalizability claims."
